==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|prender}}, from {{inh|pt|la|prendere}}, variant of {{m|la|prehendere}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|prehendō||I seize; I detain}}, from {{m|la|prae-||before}} + {{m|la|*hendō||I take, seize}} (not attested without prefix), from {{der|pt|ine-pro|*gʰed-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Paulista}} {{IPA|/pɾẽ.ˈde(ɹ)/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|/pɾẽ.ˈde(ɻ)/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/pɾẽ.ˈdeɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|pren|der|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|pre|nder}}

# to [[arrest]] (to seize and take into legal custody)
# to [[attach]] or [[bind]]
# to [[restrain]]; to [[restrict]]
# to become [[close]] (emotionally) to someone

====Conjugation====
{{pt-conj|pre|nder}}

